 "note": "hands v2 (2026-10-13), for hands_v2_post.py / hands_v2_field.py, appended after P-earroot2, in place of hands v1. Anatomy review 2026-10-13, finding 8 (Nick, 2026-10-13: \"Yes, fix all ten of them.\"); coordinator review of v1 (2026-10-13): claws came out of the gaps beside the digits with their cut tops showing, bunched from the front, digits small lumps, palm pad with a lip edge. The +x paw is described; the step runs one grid per paw and mirrors every mass to -x. blurs and erode: the old lumps, palm ridges and crease band averaged out, the paw end pulled in .005. toes: one tapered capsule per toe, fuller at the tip (rb .017) than at the knuckle (ra .013), narrower across the row (ySquash 1.95), splayed -9, -3, 3, 9 degrees, joined toe to toe (toeToeK) and to the paw (toeK). pads: palm pad and four toe pads, plus a nail-bed hood on the back of each toe tip over the claw root, all flattened ellipsoids joined by a smooth minimum (no edge). claws: per fore claw a rotation about its base (pivot) so it points along its toe, curled 15 degrees toward the palm, then a translation that seats its base .0075 inside its toe tip, centered on the toe, 30 degrees toward the back of the toe (mirrored for -x). sheath: a claw-shaped collar joined to the skin was tried (v2a to v2h) and folded the coarse skin mesh in the valleys; it is off (collar -1) and the nail-bed hood is the fold instead. preSmooth (with alongNormal), relax, untangle, finalUnfold, postSmooth: the mover settings that put the old lumpy vertices onto the new toes without folds (see hands_v2_field.move_vertices_from and taubin). Development variants v2a to v2l in untracked anatomy-fixes/work/08-hands/specs (this is v2l, from gen3.py). World units, +y back.",
